        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-129146",
        ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}m+5n &=11 \\\\ 0 &=4n-8 \\\\ n &=-6m+\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $m,n$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}m+5n &=11 \\\\ 0m-4n &=-8 \\\\ 6m+n &=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}\\frac{1}{3} & 5 & 11 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 6 & 1 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"
